speechtext:
Oh, earlier than that;
considerably earlier. I was not here, you know, when the ship sailed. That is the finding against the quartermaster-general's branch. I come back to what I said originally, and the summing up of it is that the commissioner finds that Colonel Spearing, by not exercising due diligence on October 9 or 10, and not ascertaining the capacity of the Awatea was himself negligent, or showed a lack of energy, and he then contributed to these vehicles not having gone.
There are a lot of things to be said with regard to that. I must say that when the matter came to my attention first, and I am not sure that it is not my opinion to-day- and I say this frankly-I considered that it was lack of good staff work rather than anything really affecting the Hong Kong expedition.
